  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the points be $A(-2,4,7)$ and $B(3,-5,8)$ on $Y Z$-plane, $x$-coordinate $=0$.<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/U3gdRe4rjERxY6nARZ6_prnRjGEwHH0AQrCCMdLDNDM.original.fullsize.png\"><br><br />Let the ratio be $K: 1$. <br />The coordinates of $C$ are $\\left(\\frac{3 K-2}{K+1}, \\frac{-5 K+4}{K+1}, \\frac{8 K+7}{K+1}\\right)$<br />Clearly $\\frac{3 K-2}{K+1}=0 \\Rightarrow 3 K=2 \\Rightarrow K=\\frac{2}{3}$ <br />Hence required ratio is $2: 3$.",
    "image": null
  },
